    {
      "sourceLine": 3,
      "title": "The morning hour and Kellan’s card",
      "direction": "Monday quarter to seven replaces the evening hour explicitly. Kiva is recovering, not miraculously well. Kellan’s card is a personal request for an honest clerk, not foundation employment. Six pumps times six minutes times fifty-seven is 2052; let each factor land. He chooses the low town while knowing the Step risk. Dray advises an independent watch, still unpersuaded."
    },
    {
      "sourceLine": 65,
      "title": "The price said before",
      "direction": "Aske at quarter past seven: hand warm eight mornings, pulse ninety. Seventh forecast remains five or six nights; second crossing in one hour is an honest untested guess, hand to wrist and weeks, then fortnight rate. Ten dark counts separate crossing from fresh lighting. Conditional consequences must sound conditional, not a prediction of Wednesday’s events."
    },
    {
      "sourceLine": 89,
      "title": "Names on the warrant",
      "direction": "Monday nine, voluntary signatures. Read nonparticipation and loses nothing without disapproval. Perrin declares captain and brake, not mud work. Jude steadies with left and writes with right; Pru’s blush never childish. Kiva offers caller only if officer accepts. Dray stands on healed leg; no friendship or conversion implied."
    },
    {
      "sourceLine": 137,
      "title": "A bucket explained",
      "direction": "Pump-hall meeting, lifted clarity without shouting over imagined effects. Yeo holds the warrant, Mara method, Peverell house, Hart slack. Coombe asks a repeatable explanation. Brask corrects bucket to cask, staves and chime, held water its head. Twenty-minute window and order are separate: move expression into Graving and secure it before quenching cells. Rusk’s six corrects Ferren’s eight; no mocking incompetence."
    },
    {
      "sourceLine": 195,
      "title": "Two masters’ proposed work",
      "direction": "Halden’s Step can hold pumps only until Mara says salt; Rusk demands Tuesday demonstration. Sister reports Thrale’s forty-pace suppression and hour limit. Master waits clear until last plant, then holds mouth; M3 forty-five paces in. These are plans, not tested guarantees; sister does not confirm Kiva’s inference about harbour pressure."
    },
    {
      "sourceLine": 245,
      "title": "The pass and responsibility",
      "direction": "Kiva proposes three planks of like doors, unlike doors between phases. Three passes, each under fifty paces; test every mark first. Reserve Ember-to-still crossing certified once; second failure cost only conditional. Yeo’s professionals close tear; students cut only on her slate. Far edge named before each pass. Eighteen strangers require rehearsal; the caller’s limits are still the current sheet’s limits."
    },
    {
      "sourceLine": 289,
      "title": "Learning to release",
      "direction": "Monday afternoon tun drill. Catch, carry and plant work individually; release call fails because trained hands wait for agreement. Treen’s apparent success is the forbidden overlap; a wooden tun tolerates what living load will not. Carrow identifies learned habit. Coombe’s rope teaches letting go into air before receiving hand catches. End with shared call and teachable method, no ownership triumph. Tun is rehearsal only and tomorrow must expose its missing behavior."
    }
  ],
